#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fleet-watch — merge is ignition (plan 0004, roadmap row 6b).

One poll cycle: scan allowlisted, branch-protected repos ON MAIN ONLY for
feature plans that are `status: ready` and carry no implbot-authored PR (in
ANY state) marked `Plan: <id>`, then spawn one orchestrator per such plan, up
to the concurrency cap.

The watcher is MECHANICAL: it never edits a repo, never talks to a model, and
never acts on staleness. It spawns, it emits, it notifies. Everything
judgment-shaped lives in bin/orchestrator.

Why main-only: reachability on `main` IS the authorisation. `fleet-plan lint`
is a validity check, not an authorisation check — only a human's reviewed merge
produces reachability, so merging a plan file is the ignition and no separate
arm step exists. "Human" is enforced, not assumed (r6 M2, revised by ADR-0004 2026-09-09):
main_is_protected refuses any repo where an agent account could PUSH or MERGE
main, because either writes it outright. Approving is a THRESHOLD, not a write,
so agents may hold approval rights provided they cannot reach
`required_approvals` between them — one agent against two required means a human
approval is structurally mandatory, which Forgejo's scheduled auto-merge cannot
route around. A `ready` plan on an unmerged branch is invisible here by design.

Config (env; the allowlist has NO default — an unconfigured watcher dispatches
nothing):
  FLEET_WATCH_REPOS     comma list, e.g. "operator/sniff,operator/ares"
  FLEET_WATCH_CAP       max concurrent orchestrators (default 1)
  FLEET_OPERATOR_UID     numeric Forgejo user id whose `respawn` comment counts
  FLEET_IMPLEMENTER_UIDS  comma list of numeric uids whose work PRs mark a plan
                        as dispatched. Preferred over logins: dedupe gates
                        SPEND, and a rename must not silently re-ignite every
                        merged plan (r7 M2).
  FLEET_IMPLEMENTER_LOGINS  comma list, fallback when no uid is configured
                        (default "implbot")
  FLEET_AGENT_ACCOUNTS  *** SET THIS ON THE BROKER, NOT HERE. *** Comma list of
                        ADDITIONAL automated accounts that must never be able to
                        push or merge main, and that count toward the approvals
                        SUFFICIENCY test rather than being banned from it
                        (ADR-0004, revised), merged with the built-in
                        author/reviewer accounts (r7 L5). Since ADR-0003 §2 it is
                        read by main_is_protected, which runs in the BROKER's
                        process on vaulthost — setting it here is a silent no-op and
                        fails OPEN: a repo whose merge whitelist holds the extra
                        account comes back ok:true and gets vouched for. It
                        belongs on keyvault's
                        net.operator.keyvault-forgejo-broker.plist.
  FLEET_AUTHOR_ACCOUNT / FLEET_REVIEWER_ACCOUNT / FLEET_MERGER_ACCOUNT
                        rename the three positions (plan 0056) for a deployment
                        whose forge accounts are not called implbot,
                        revbot and operator. Defaults are this fleet's own
                        accounts; see fleetlib.agent_roles() and
                        docs/operating.md's mapping. The three POSITIONS
                        (author/reviewer/merger) are not configurable, only
                        the names filling them.
  FLEET_FORGEJO_URL     READ IN BOTH PLACES, and they are not the same read.
                        Default http://forge.example:3000. THIS host's value
                        is what every call the watcher still makes uses —
                        plans/ listings, plan bodies, the dedupe PR scan,
                        respawn comments — so keep it set here. The BROKER's
                        own copy decides which Forgejo the protection VERDICT
                        comes from, because main_is_protected runs in its
                        process. Only the verdict moved. Set both, and set them
                        to the same instance.
  FLEET_VERDICT_SOURCE  "broker" (default) or "direct" — which implementation
                        answers "is main protected" (plan 0054). Broker is the
                        default for a reason: this fleet is multi-host, and an
                        unconfigured watcher must not silently gain a stronger
                        credential than it is handed. "direct" is for a
                        deployment where the watcher, the forge credential and
                        the repository already share one trust boundary; see
                        docs/plan-dispatch.md for what it costs. Selection is
                        never a runtime fallback — an unreachable broker stays
                        "could not determine" and does not fall through.
  FLEET_DIRECT_TOKEN_CMD  command printing an ADMIN-scoped Forgejo token, read
                        only when FLEET_VERDICT_SOURCE=direct. No default:
                        FLEET_TOKEN_CMD's own default helper is write-scoped
                        and 403s on branch_protections, and this fleet does
                        not hand out an admin-scoped helper by default.
  FLEET_BROKER_SOCKET   local unix socket reaching keyvault's forgejo-broker
                        (default ~/run/forgejo-broker.sock). An ssh forward puts
                        vaulthost's socket there today; a SPIFFE sidecar will later.
                        Read only when FLEET_VERDICT_SOURCE=broker (the default).
  FLEET_BROKER_TIMEOUT  seconds to wait for a verdict (default 90 — the broker's
                        cold-cache worst case, not the expectation)
  FLEET_TOKEN_CMD       command printing a Forgejo token (default
                        ~/bin/fetch-forgejo-token.sh — the sanctioned helper;
                        the token is never logged, echoed, or spooled)
  FLEET_ORCHESTRATOR    orchestrator path (default: sibling bin/orchestrator)
  FLEET_NTFY_URL        push endpoint for surfaced conditions
  FLEET_PR_PAGE_CAP     list-scan bound (default 20 pages x 50)
  FLEET_PINS            comma list of DETACHED worktree paths whose HEAD should
                        equal their own origin/main, e.g.
                        "~/.local/share/pins/eunomia,~/.local/share/pins/techne".
                        No default: an unconfigured watcher checks no pins, the
                        same rule FLEET_WATCH_REPOS follows. Reported only --
                        the watcher never moves a pin (see check_pins).
  FLEET_PIN_ADVANCE_PLIST  path to the INSTALLED fleet-pin-advance plist (plan
                        0059), read once per process for its `StartInterval` --
                        the window a self-healing stale pin is given before
                        `check_pins` pages on it. Default
                        ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-pin-advance.plist,
                        the installed copy, not this repo's launchd/ one: the
                        installed one is what actually runs and the two can
                        differ. Overridable so a result never depends on
                        whether the machine running the suite happens to have
                        the unit installed -- the suite always sets this.
  FLEET_PIN_PAGE_MARGIN  extra seconds added to that window before paging
                        (plan 0059; default 600) -- must exceed the watcher's
                        own poll jitter, or a sample taken moments before the
                        advancer's next run would misread a healthy pin as
                        overdue.
"""
import datetime as _dt
import argparse
import fnmatch
import http.client
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import hashlib
import os
import plistlib
import re
import socket
import signal
import subprocess
import time
import sys
import urllib.request
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

